      "writtenOn": "2023-12-19T00:19:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "do we know if there is measurable performance impact to this additional instrumentation?",
      "revId": "5fcb8ec01e7c85a58edc62544d45a3ba1aa78c0f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c3f4489b_3ddf20b1",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1557540
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-19T00:24:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t know the impact. I\u0027m blindly adding it as it\u0027s included in previous GKI kernels and expected by our vintf checks:\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:kernel/configs/v/android-6.6/android-base.config;l\u003d55?q\u003dv%2Fandroid-6.6%2Fandroid-base.config\n\nIt got removed from android-mainline implicitly which is what v6.6 was based off of. The options are either add it back to the gki_defconfig or remove it from the vintf config.",
      "parentUuid": "9eb8b4d7_da611f8d",
      "revId": "5fcb8ec01e7c85a58edc62544d45a3ba1aa78c0f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "285ac235_b985a274",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-19T00:31:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "should it be re-enabled in android-mainline?",
      "parentUuid": "c3f4489b_3ddf20b1",
      "revId": "5fcb8ec01e7c85a58edc62544d45a3ba1aa78c0f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ab973713_41d4f31d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1557540
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-19T00:40:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question. Based on https://r.android.com/1270721, I would say yes; however, I\u0027m not entirely sure the same logic applies after https://lore.kernel.org/all/20230811151847.1594958-4-elver@google.com/. Was the original thinking that we need `DEBUG_LIST` to enable `BUG_ON_DATA_CORRUPTION`? If so, do we still need `DEBUG_LIST` now that `BUG_ON_DATA_CORRUPTION` doesn\u0027t require/select it?\n\nThoughts @gregkh@google.com?",
      "parentUuid": "285ac235_b985a274",
      "revId": "5fcb8ec01e7c85a58edc62544d45a3ba1aa78c0f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f2e9af81_3dc3c624",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-19T08:40:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t know, @keescook@google.com would be the best one to answer this.",
      "parentUuid": "ab973713_41d4f31d",
      "revId": "5fcb8ec01e7c85a58edc62544d45a3ba1aa78c0f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "005c4c8a_5e24df86",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1082649
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-11T16:29:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We definitely want `DEBUG_LIST` enabled -- this trivially catches list corruption issues that would otherwise allow for some classic exploitation primitives. I haven\u0027t done a performance analysis in a long time, but when I last looked at it, it was totally in the noise (there just aren\u0027t a lot of heavy list manipulation hot paths).\n\nThe question about `BUG_ON_DATA_CORRUPTION` is more about the policy on handling kernel issues. If we set `panic_on_warn`, then we don\u0027t need it (same result). If we don\u0027t, then it\u0027s a question of \"do we want the device to keep running in the face of a detected memory corruption?\" With my paranoid hat on, I think we should panic, but I can see there might be other opinions. 😊\n\nPerhaps @jeffv@google.com can answer the policy question?",
      "parentUuid": "f2e9af81_3dc3c624",
      "revId": "5fcb8ec01e7c85a58edc62544d45a3ba1aa78c0f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2b017c82_f3380a00",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1557540
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-11T17:17:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With regards to `DEBUG_LIST`, do we still need it for v6.6 now that `LIST_HARDENED` has been introduced and doesn\u0027t depend on `DEBUG_LIST`? Refer to https://lore.kernel.org/all/20230811151847.1594958-3-elver@google.com/ which seems to indicate that we can get a throughput perf improvement of ~7%.\n\nRegarding `BUG_ON_DATA_CORRUPTION`, since that config has been enabled for some time now, I\u0027ll keep it set.",
      "parentUuid": "005c4c8a_5e24df86",
      "revId": "5fcb8ec01e7c85a58edc62544d45a3ba1aa78c0f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d5e3ffb8_e6ff0405",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1082649
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-18T18:33:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah! Sorry, I missed we were talking about v6.6 Yes, I think `LIST_HARDENED` has sufficient coverage compared to `DEBUG_LIST`. If performance is an issue here, I\u0027m comfortable with choosing `LIST_HARDENED` over `DEBUG_LIST`.",
      "parentUuid": "2b017c82_f3380a00",
      "revId": "5fcb8ec01e7c85a58edc62544d45a3ba1aa78c0f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
